  "id": "COMPOUND:21359 - PROTEIN:6319",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Euphorbiaproliferin F may interact with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Euphorbiaproliferin F to CWR22R, which is then targeted by 3Alpha,24,29-Trihydroxyolean-12-En-28-Oic Acid, a compound that directly targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. The second pathway connects Euphorbiaproliferin F to C-C motif chemokine 8, which is targeted by Gorgost-5-en-3-ol, another compound that also targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. The third pathway involves Euphorbiaproliferin F targeting CWR22R, which is then targeted by Mycalenitrile 13, which also acts on UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. These findings collectively indicate that Euphorbiaproliferin F may influence UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly through the activation of downstream signaling pathways or by modulating the activity of compounds that target this enzyme. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a potential role for Euphorbiaproliferin F in modulating UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
